{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_58ce97d8c35b4d7e9e7314ba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The docs file `docs/task-flow-and-failure-semantics.md` doesn't exist. The context mentions it but it's missing. That's fine — the requirements are clear enough. The key point from the context is: TargetVault is a routing field on the command struct, NOT a frontmatter key; do not add it to any Updates map.\n\nNow let me understand the task:\n\n1. Bump dependency to `github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.86.0`. The requirement says: \"Run this AFTER the code importing the new field exists or in the same step — the import must be written before `go mod tidy` demotes the dep.\"\n\n2. Add helper `targetVaultFromTask` in pkg/result_publisher.go that reads the task's frontmatter key \"target_vault\" and returns it as a string, returning \"\" when absent or not a string. The `TaskFrontmatter.String(key)` method does exactly this — returns `(\"\", false)` when absent or not a string. So `targetVaultFromTask` can use `task.Frontmatter.String(\"target_vault\")`.\n\n3. Populate TargetVault from that helper in all six command constructions:\n   - PublishSpawnNotification (UpdateFrontmatterCommand)\n   - PublishFailure's update command (UpdateFrontmatterCommand)\n   - PublishFailure's increment command (IncrementFrontmatterCommand)\n   - PublishIncrementTriggerCount (IncrementFrontmatterCommand)\n   - PublishSetTriggerScope (UpdateFrontmatterCommand)\n   - PublishTypeMismatchFailure (UpdateFrontmatterCommand)\n\n4. Tests: publish with task whose frontmatter carries target_vault: \"personal\" → captured update AND increment payloads decode with TargetVault \"personal\"; publish with task lacking key → payloads decode with empty TargetVault (field absent on wire).\n\n5. Existing tests keep passing where fixture has no target_vault key (omitempty keeps wire shape stable).\n\n6. CHANGELOG entry under `## Unreleased`.\n\nLet me check the changelog-guid